⚡🇱🇧🇮🇱 Lebanon's Internal Security Forces Information Branch says it arrested Fouad Khalifeh about two weeks ago, minutes before he tried to leave the country, after months of surveillance. A Lebanese security source says the operation was carried out entirely by Lebanese authorities, without cooperation from any Arab security service.

Khalifeh is accused of giving Israel intelligence on Hezbollah figures, tracking people of security significance, and collecting information through a hospital on patients wounded in the pager attacks. He is the latest Shiite suspect accused of spying for Israel, following the arrests of Mohammad Saleh and Ahmad Al-Mokhader.

